  "description": "Redevelopment of the site to include demolition of no. 229 and Pocock House, erection of a purpose built student accommodation building (Sui Generis), retention and remodeling of nos. 231 and 233 to provide flexible commercial/community floorspace (Class E / Class F1 / Class F2), with associated public realm, access, car parking, cycle parking, hard and soft landscaping and other ancillary works. \r\r For information only: \r- The proposed PBSA building including additional rooftop plant/enclosure is Maximum 150.655m AOD/147.055m above ground and is 45 storeys. \rThe maximum height of the remodeling of Nos 231 and 233 is 18.745m AOD/15.145m above ground.\rThe development as a whole comprises:\r- 798 bedrooms:  851 bedspaces  \r- 255 sqm GIA of flexible commercial, learning and non-residential institution floorspace (Class E / F1/F2 use);\rThe application is accompanied by an Environmental Statement (ES) in accordance with the Town and Country Planning (Environmental Impact Assessment) Regulations 2017 (as amended). This can be viewed on  Southwark Council's Public Access for Planning Register. Hard copies of the ES are available for inspection at the John Harvard Library, 211 Borough High St, London SE1 1JA (Monday to Friday 9am to 7pm, Saturday 9am-5pm). Hard copies can also be purchased from DP9 Ltd\r100 Pall Mall, London, SW1Y 5NQ, telephone: 020 7004 1700 \r",
